    "title": "Two men arrested in Cullman in Marshall County theft - NewsBreak",
    "text": "MARSHALL COUNTY, Ala (WHNT) — The Marshall County Sheriff’s Office says two men were arrested last month in Cullman in connection with the theft of a tractor and trailer in Marshall County. The sheriff’s office said that on June 25, it received a call from the Cullman Police Department regarding a stolen tractor and trailer taken out of Marshall County. According to MCSO, CPD said they were on a call regarding stolen property at the Cullman Walmart. According to authorities, police were notified that the tractor and trailer had been in the parking lot for a couple of days, and the people who brought it there were on their way to pick the items up. MCSO said deputies and Cullman police set up at the tractor and trailer to wait for the men, but the pair called Walmart, saying they had broken down on Interstate 65. The sheriff’s office said that at that point, CPD made contact with the men on the side of I-65. MCSO said the two men were identified as Kenneth Elliot and Matthew Allen. The sheriff’s office said after interviews, the two men were arrested and taken to the Marshall County Jail for booking. MCSO said the stolen property was returned to its owner. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WHNT.com.",
